Title: The Salt Road
Credit: Written by
Author: A. Draft
Draft date: 2026-08-04

FADE IN:

INT. SALT WORKS - DAY

Steam over the evaporation pans. MAREN, 40s, walks the boards with a
rake balanced on one shoulder.

MAREN
It never dries out here. Not properly.

TOBIAS (O.S.)
That's the point of it.

Tobias climbs the ladder from the lower pan, gloves soaked through.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
(wiping his hands)
Third time this week the pump's cut out.

MAREN
Then we rake it by hand.

TOBIAS
We did that in eighty-nine.

MAREN
And it worked in eighty-nine.

They stand a moment. Wind moves across the pans.

CUT TO:

EXT. SALT WORKS - CAUSEWAY - CONTINUOUS

A thin road of packed salt, water either side, running to the mainland.

MAREN (V.O.)
My father walked this every morning for thirty years.

.A SLUGLINE FORCED WITH A PERIOD

The causeway narrows. A cart has stopped halfway, one wheel off the edge.

MAREN
(calling)
Leave it! Tide's coming!

DRIVER
It's the whole load!

MAREN                    TOBIAS
Leave the load!          It's not worth it!

> CENTERED TEXT <

[[A production note that should not print.]]

= A synopsis line for the scene.

INT. FARMHOUSE - NIGHT

Maren at the table, ledger open, counting nothing.

MAREN
(to herself)
Eighty-nine.

FADE OUT.

THE END
